{"description":"Name or text of the contract being verified.","type":"string"},"criteria":{"description":"The contract's criteria; at least one is required.","type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"description":"Criterion id; must be non-empty and unique; evidence refers to it.","type":"string"},"description":{"description":"What the criterion requires.","type":"string"},"min_strength":{"description":"Minimum evidence strength: `strong` refuses weak passes; empty or `weak` accepts any strength.","type":"string"}},"required":["id","description","min_strength"]}},"evidence":{"description":"Deterministic observations supplied by the caller; each must name a declared criterion.","type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"criterion":{"description":"Id of the declared criterion this observation is evidence for.","type":"string"},"source":{"description":"Where the observation came from, e.g. the check that ran.","type":"string"},"result":{"description":"What the check reported: `pass`, `fail` (needs detail) or `verifier_error` (says nothing about the work).","type":"string"},"strength":{"description":"Evidence strength: `weak` or `strong`; empty means strong.","type":"string"},"detail":{"description":"Explanation of the result; required when result is `fail`.","type":"string"},"passes_on_known_bad_basis":{"default":false,"description":"True when the check also passed against a basis known to be wrong, so its pass cannot tell good work from bad. Default false.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["criterion","source","result","strength","detail"]}},"execution_completed":{"default":false,"description":"What the executor claimed; read and ignored, never evidence. Default false.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["contract","criteria","evidence"]},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"}},{"name":"agentmux_capability_wait","description":"Block until something this process owns can settle, so a caller with no other work stops polling; or arm a durable wait that fires on a machine event even after this session ends.\n\naction is `wait` (the default; `{}` is the whole call), `arm`, `status`, or `cancel`. `status` only reads; `wait` marks the fired arm it reports delivered; `arm` and `cancel` write records under ~/.local/state/capability-waits and load or unload user LaunchAgents.\n\n`wait`: settles on the first of: a report-back record the channel store holds for this session (a background completion the notify chain wrote, one adopted from a dead session at boot, or a chat tunnel addressed to it), a background job of this process that is not running, an arm this process made that fired, or an atask task that becomes complete during the wait. A job already stopped, or an arm already fired, when the call begins settles immediately; each fire settles one wait. A task already complete when the call starts does not. There is no caller-selectable timeout. status is `settled` (carries completion {id, subject, from, about?}, job {job_id, state, exit_code?}, wait {wait_id, state, until, outcome?}, or task {id, title}), `nothing_to_wait_for`, or `timed_out`. `nothing_to_wait_for` returns at once when no report-back record is pending for this session, no job is listed, no arm of this process is live, and every listed task has already finished. `timed_out` is the 30-minute cap; elapsed_ms says how long the call waited. Sources are re-read every 500 ms. If you started a job with `bash` and this returns `nothing_to_wait_for`, poll that job with `bash_status` instead of calling wait again.\n\n`arm`: { until, on_fire, escalate?, ttl?, one_shot? } returns status `armed` with wait_id at once, or `refused` with the fix. until is one of { type: disk_mounted, volume }, { type: path_changed, path }, { type: timer, seconds | at: { hour, minute?, weekday? } }, { type: job_exit, job_id }, { type: job_output, log_path }, { type: process_exit, pid }. on_fire is { notify: true }, { command }, or { worker: { prompt } } (files an atask draft and runs a headless worker). one_shot requires ttl (30s, 10m, 2h, 1d); if the event has not come by then, escalate runs instead, else the arm expires. An arm is refused when its predicate is already true at arm time (mounted volume, exited pid) or its on_fire/escalate command fails the same refusals `run_command` applies; a calendar `timer at` recurs and always arms. disk_mounted fires once unless `repeat: true`; exit ticks run every 30 s and pin the process start time; records are 0600, and the fire path claims the record exclusively so two simultaneous fires run on_fire once. Arming installs one sweep LaunchAgent (every 300 s) that fires missed edges, marks crashed fires `fire_failed`, and deletes terminal records after 7 days.\n\n`status`: with wait_id, status `found` and the arm; without, status `listed` and the newest 100. `cancel` { wait_id }: unloads it, status `cancelled`. An unknown wait_id is `not_found`.\n\nExample: {\"action\":\"arm\",\"until\":{\"type\":\"disk_mounted\",\"volume\":\"Backup\"},\"on_fire\":{\"command\":\"rsync -a ~/work /Volumes/Backup\"}}.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"action":{"default":"wait","description":"wait (default) blocks this turn; arm is durable and returns wait_id at once; status and cancel manage arms","type":"string","enum":["wait","arm","status","cancel"]},"until":{"description":"arm: the event it settles on","oneOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","const":"disk_mounted"},"volume":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Volume name under /Volumes, e.g. `Time Machine`"},"repeat":{"description":"Fire on every mount; the default retires the arm after one fire","type":"boolean"}},"required":["type","volume"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","const":"path_changed"},"path":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Absolute path to watch; it must exist when the arm is made"}},"required":["type","path"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","const":"timer"},"seconds":{"description":"Fire every N seconds","type":"integer","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991},"at":{"description":"Fire daily at this local time","type":"object","properties":{"hour":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":23},"minute":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":59},"weekday":{"description":"0 and 7 are Sunday","type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":6}},"required":["hour"]}},"required":["type"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","const":"job_exit"},"job_id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"A background job this process started"}},"required":["type","job_id"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","const":"job_output"},"log_path":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The job's log file, watched for new output"}},"required":["type","log_path"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","const":"process_exit"},"pid":{"type":"integer","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991}},"required":["type","pid"]}]},"on_fire":{"description":"arm: what runs when it fires","anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"notify":{"type":"boolean","const":true,"description":"Mark fired; the session's next `wait` settles on it"}},"required":["notify"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"command":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Shell command to run when it fires"}},"required":["command"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"worker":{"type":"object","properties":{"prompt":{"type":"string","minLength":1}},"required":["prompt"],"description":"File an atask draft and run a headless worker on it"}},"required":["worker"]}]},"escalate":{"description":"arm: runs instead when a one-shot's ttl expires undelivered","anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"notify":{"type":"boolean","const":true,"description":"Mark fired; the session's next `wait` settles on it"}},"required":["notify"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"command":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Shell command to run when it fires"}},"required":["command"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"worker":{"type":"object","properties":{"prompt":{"type":"string","minLength":1}},"required":["prompt"],"description":"File an atask draft and run a headless worker on it"}},"required":["worker"]}]},"ttl":{"description":"arm: how late is too late, e.g. 30m; required with one_shot","type":"string","pattern":"^\\d+(s|m|h|d)$"},"one_shot":{"description":"arm: fire at most once; requires ttl","type":"boolean"},"wait_id":{"description":"status / cancel: the arm; status without it lists every arm","type":"string","minLength":1}}},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"}},{"name":"agentmux_capability_web_search","description":"Search the web for current facts, docs, or versions and return ranked results with titles, URLs, and snippets. Read-only and never cached: the answer is the live web. Use it for something this repo cannot know; use `grep` or `find` for this codebase.\n\nCall: { query, limit? }. query is what to look up. limit is at most this many results, default 5. Provider is chosen at call time: OpenRouter's web plugin when OPENROUTER_API_KEY is set, else DuckDuckGo's keyless lite endpoint. A failed provider falls through to the next. The answer names the provider used. A provider HTTP failure throws `HTTP <status>: <body>`. No provider available is an error, not an empty result list.\n\nExample: {\"query\":\"ast-grep pattern metavariable syntax\",\"limit\":5}.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"What to look up"},"limit":{"default":5,"description":"At most this many results; default 5","type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":10}},"required":["query"]},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"}},{"name":"agentmux_capability_webmaster.page.audit","description":"Audit one live page across areas by running each area's capability, judge what the page is for (zwsip's purpose, sections and interpretation stages), then rank all findings together and summarize the page's health. Registered as `webmaster.page.audit`. Use `webmaster.page.seo` or `webmaster.page.performance` when you only need one area, or the purpose, sections and interpretation capabilities for one judgment stage alone.\n\nCall: { url, site?, site_context?, areas?, measurements? }. areas defaults to [\"seo\", \"performance\"] and names the rule areas only; the judgment stages always run. An area that throws is rethrown as `audit <area> of <url>: <cause>`. An unmeasured content probe does not fail the audit: the judgment stages degrade to `not auditable` and the reason is recorded in summary.unmeasured as area `content`. summary.health is healthy, needs_attention, critical, or unknown when every area came back unmeasured. The answer is { url, areas, judgment, findings, summary } with finding counts. It does not edit the page.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"Address of the page to audit."},"site":{"description":"A site name under `webmaster/sites/`; the CLI resolves it into `site_context`.","type":"string"},"site_context":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"Site name, as in its `webmaster/sites/<site>.yaml` file."},"url":{"type":"string","description":"The site's home address."},"host":{"type":"string","description":"Host name of `url`."},"tier":{"description":"The site's tier label, when its site file sets one.","type":"string"},"platform":{"description":"The platform the site runs on, when its site file sets one.","type":"string"},"probe_paths":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Paths the site's own probes measure; `/` by default."},"priva