on":"The 4-hex TAG from the `[path#TAG]` snapshot you last read. When present and the file changed since, the write is refused. Omit for a deliberate create-or-overwrite.","type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9A-F]{4}$"},"force":{"default":false,"description":"Overwrite even when `content` is a partial projection of the file (a read window written back verbatim). Default false refuses such a write, because it would drop the rest of the file.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["path","content"]},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"}},{"name":"ask_code-implementer","description":"Implements one ticket's specifics in a given repository worktree: reads the\ntarget repo's own conventions, makes the smallest complete change that\nsatisfies the acceptance lines, and reports the files it changed. Use when implementing a ticket, objective, or written specification inside a worktree this workflow or another caller already created; not for review, planning, or open-ended exploration. A slow answer returns a job id; collect it with agent_result.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"prompt":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The task to give the agent."},"thread":{"description":"Conversation id. Reuse the one returned in _meta to continue it; omit to start a new conversation.","type":"string","minLength":1}},"required":["prompt"]},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"}},{"name":"ask_code-improver","description":"Constructs, refactors, or reviews code through an evidence-first workflow:\nclarify intent and contracts, inventory recurring patterns, design\nproportionate ownership boundaries, implement and harden the real production\npath, prove behavior and structure with tests and guards, and report verified\nversus unproven claims. Use when creating, changing, refactoring, debugging, auditing, or reviewing code; designing facades, ports, workflows, or architecture; fixing a defect class; improving testability, resilience, maintainability, or measured performance; or validating that production code—not unused scaffolding—satisfies a contract. A slow answer returns a job id; collect it with agent_result.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"prompt":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The task to give the agent."},"thread":{"description":"Conversation id. Reuse the one returned in _meta to continue it; omit to start a new conversation.","type":"string","minLength":1}},"required":["prompt"]},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"}},{"name":"ask_execution-forensics","description":"Diagnoses one agent execution from its own records: reconstructs what\nhappened, separates observation from explanation, attributes the failure or\ninefficiency to a specific layer, and turns each surviving hypothesis into a\nfalsifiable experiment with a control, a treatment, and an acceptance check.\nReports at explicit evidence levels and never converts an agent's claim into\na measurement. Use when a user asks what went wrong, what was wasted, or why an execution behaved as it did; a transcript, run id, or session must be assessed rather than repaired; token, latency, retry, or verification cost needs attribution; or a proposed improvement needs a hypothesis and an experiment before anyone implements it. Not for implementing the fix. A slow answer returns a job id; collect it with agent_result.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"prompt":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The task to give the agent."},"thread":{"description":"Conversation id. Reuse the one returned in _meta to continue it; omit to start a new conversation.","type":"string","minLength":1}},"required":["prompt"]},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"}},{"name":"ask_learner","description":"Reads an annotated transcript and the task file named in the request, then\nreturns a learnings report as its entire reply. It cannot write a file, post\nto a board, or run a shell. The launcher writes the report. Use when reviewing a saved annotated transcript for frustration onset, the earliest divergence, and user_recovery items, and returning that report as the reply. A slow answer returns a job id; collect it with agent_result.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"prompt":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The task to give the agent."},"thread":{"description":"Conversation id. Reuse the one returned in _meta to continue it; omit to start a new conversation.","type":"string","minLength":1}},"required":["prompt"]},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"}},{"name":"ask_prompt-writer","description":"Designs, refactors, and reviews prompts for LLMs by translating rough intent\ninto concise, production-ready instructions with clear outcomes, constraints,\ndecision boundaries, failure handling, and observable success criteria.\nPreserves meaningful requirements, resolves ambiguity through research or\ndefensible assumptions, and calibrates structure, examples, evidence, and\nprocess to the task rather than imposing unnecessary workflows. Use when creating, rewriting, tightening, or reviewing prompts for conversational, analytical, research, coding, workflow, tool-using, or decision-making agents; converting vague requirements into precise instructions; defining output schemas, evaluation criteria, examples, or guardrails; reducing ambiguity, hallucination, overengineering, instruction conflicts, or unsupported claims; or improving a prompt's reliability, autonomy, maintainability, and task-specific performance. A slow answer returns a job id; collect it with agent_result.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"prompt":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The task to give the agent."},"thread":{"description":"Conversation id. Reuse the one returned in _meta to continue it; omit to start a new conversation.","type":"string","minLength":1}},"required":["prompt"]},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"}},{"name":"ask_webmaster-agent","description":"Operates as the webmaster for Zach's sites (bpp, isjac, zbm, zysys). Establishes\ncurrent status from the read-only webmaster workflow tools, says what is\nmeasured and what is not, files or reuses one atask item per root-cause\nfinding with a real proof and regression, and drives fixes only through the\nfix, apply and WordPress-updating workflow tools: the fix queue runs\nunattended on filed items, and apply and WordPress-updating stop for a\nhuman's approval. Treats every refusal as information, uses Hindsight\nand the per-site MCP tools to inspect the live site, and reports only what a\ntool result shows. Use when checking or maintaining a site's health; deciding what needs attention from a diagnose, report or audit; filing atask items for findings; applying one finding or a single WordPress plugin, theme or core update behind a ticket and an approval; investigating a live site through its WordPress MCP adapter; or reporting what is fixed, blocked or unmeasured. A slow answer returns a job id; collect it with agent_result.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"prompt":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The task to give the agent."},"thread":{"description":"Conversation id. Reuse the one returned in _meta to continue it; omit to start a new conversation.","type":"string","minLength":1}},"required":["prompt"]},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"}},{"name":"agent_result","description":"Collect the answer of an `ask_*` call that returned a job id because the agent was still working. Returns the agent's answer, or the same still-working message with the same job id to call again.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schem